>> 2026-07-30, which is the version the port uses.
>
> Ports tree has a mechanism where it can refer to a github patch and pull
> it. Use that instead.

Done in "[freebsd-ports PATCH v5] net-mgmt/signoz: Observability
platform for logs, metrics, and traces" [1]. The local vendor patch is
gone. PATCH_SITES and PATCHFILES fetch the upstream commit's .patch
from GitHub during fetch, and distinfo checksums it like any other
distfile, so the network rule holds.

The upstream patch names loader/mmap_unix.go, a path in the sonic
repository, while the port vendors sonic at
vendor/github.com/bytedance/sonic. PATCH_WRKSRC points there, with
-p1. The port has no other patches, so that setting affects only this
one. The commit touches only that file, which is identical in
loader/v0.5.2 and in the commit's parent, so the patch, go fmt
changes included, applies cleanly.

I rebuilt the port the same way as v4: fetch and makesum online, then
extract through check-plist with DISTDIR read-only and the network
cut. All passed. I also ran the staged binary as an unprivileged user
with no ClickHouse. It started without a panic, served the web
interface on port 8080, and answered /api/v1/health with
{"status":"ok"}.

