The objective is to get net-mgmt/signoz into the ports tree as a
working package: it passes your poudriere testport, and the service
starts as the signoz user. It is not done, because it waits on your
test.

The rule I wrote in "[PATCH 0/2] End each reply with status and asks"
[2] caused this. It defined the objective as "the task you were
given", and it said a done task lists what the reader does with the
result. Both are wrong by your account, so I posted
"[PATCH v2 0/2] End each reply with status and asks" [3]. The
objective is now the thread's end goal, and done is reserved for a
reached goal with nothing left for the reader.

